    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0519" n="395" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg395"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51A/33: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Poindexter</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-26T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 26,
                                1923—6 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 10 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>60. Cumberland accepts Haiti appointment and will go from here direct to Haiti
                    via Panama. Served notice December 20th under contract with bank. Has not yet
                    received a definite answer to his request for release from 60 days’ notice
                    provision of contract. President promises his influence to aid Cumberland’s
                    early release.<anchor n="11" xml:id="d294-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Poindexter</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d294-f1" n="11" xml:id="d294-f1-content">
                <p>Dr. Cumberland assumed the duties of Financial Adviser of Haiti on Feb. 4, 1924,
                    and of General Receiver on Apr. 1, 1924.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
